VK: list the swap chain's present mode in VkSwapchainPresentModesCreateInfoKHR.

SwapChainVK::Create chains VkSwapchainPresentScalingCreateInfoKHR when the device has
swapchainMaintenance1, but not VkSwapchainPresentModesCreateInfoKHR. Without it the swap chain
behaves as if only "presentMode" were listed, and the Khronos best-practices checks report
BestPractices-vkCreateSwapchainKHR-no-VkSwapchainPresentModesCreateInfoKHR-provided ("No
VkSwapchainPresentModesCreateInfoKHR was provided to VkCreateSwapchainKHR. When
VK_KHR_swapchain_maintenance1 is enabled, a VkSwapchainPresentModesCreateInfoKHR should be provided
to inform the implementation that the application is aware of the new features in a backward
compatible way.") for every swap chain. Measured on NRI main 72f5f46, NVIDIA, layer 1.4.341.

This chains it with the chosen present mode only, so the swap chain behaves as before.

diff --git a/Source/VK/SwapChainVK.hpp b/Source/VK/SwapChainVK.hpp
index a1fca4b4..d2ce47d8 100644
--- a/Source/VK/SwapChainVK.hpp
+++ b/Source/VK/SwapChainVK.hpp
@@ -373,6 +373,14 @@ Result SwapChainVK::Create(const SwapChainDesc& swapChainDesc) {
             PNEXTCHAIN_APPEND_STRUCT(scalingInfo);
         }
 
+        // "swapchainMaintenance1": list the present modes the swap chain may switch to (only "presentMode", NRI never switches)
+        VkSwapchainPresentModesCreateInfoKHR presentModesInfo = {VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_SWAPCHAIN_PRESENT_MODES_CREATE_INFO_KHR};
+        presentModesInfo.presentModeCount = 1;
+        presentModesInfo.pPresentModes = &presentMode;
+
+        if (m_Device.m_IsSupported.swapChainMaintenance1)
+            PNEXTCHAIN_APPEND_STRUCT(presentModesInfo);
+
         // Mutable formats
         VkFormat mutableFormats[2];
         uint32_t mutableFormatNum = 0;
